<para>
  For 9 - 12, use the following passage:
</para>
<blockquote>
  Armando’s workouts consist of kickboxing and swimming. While kickboxing, he burns 10 calories per minute and he burns 7 calories a minute while swimming. He wants to burn at least 600 calories each day.</blockquote>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="1c7c9028-047c-4202-bba8-80d3f31db857" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e80766bc-fccb-4cea-a56e-c149b0767885" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(10x + 7y ≥ 600\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(7x + 10y ≥ 600\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(7x + 10y &lt; 600\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(10x + 7y &gt; 600\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(10x + 7y ≥ 600\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>9. If <emphasis>x</emphasis> is the number of minutes that Armando will kickbox and <emphasis>y</emphasis> is the number of minutes he will swim, find the inequality that will help Armando create a workout for today.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! He burns 10x calories kickboxing and \(7y\) calories biking. The total calories must be greater than or equal to 600.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3e474b72-0161-45ff-b7af-6c6312952b34" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="b" data-solution-options="[&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;c&quot;, &quot;d&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>10. Which graph correctly represents the inequality from the previous question?</para>
      <para>a.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 60 and the \(x\)-axis at about 85. The region above the line is shaded."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/670d0e89069078484ebf1c83f05dd7378a652fa8"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>b.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at about 85 and the \(x\)-axis at 60. The region above the line is shaded."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ef2df1f537ff9c2c5fc2e38cde2e09a755329ff9"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>c.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at about 85 and the \(x\)-axis at 30. The region above the line is shaded."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5280fbc39926d829507b525ef86d6c253039d937"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>d.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 30 and the \(x\)-axis at about 85. The region above the line is shaded."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6518c9f5bae426e69157f3fd23c44ff921792c4c"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct !<figure><media alt="A graph is shown of a line crossing the \(y\)-axis at 60 and the \(x\)-axis at about 85. The region above the line is shaded."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/670d0e89069078484ebf1c83f05dd7378a652fa8"/></media></figure></para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q11-->
  <exercise data-content-id="eaf21394-aee3-4ead-9f12-cf241d847127" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(20, 70)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(20, 70)&quot;, &quot;(10, 70)&quot;, &quot;(30, 40)&quot;, &quot;(40, 20)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>11. Which of the following ordered pairs is a solution to the inequality? </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(10(20) + 7(70) = 690\), which is greater than 600.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q12-->
  <exercise data-content-id="25cf4659-a80c-4015-9524-946b2898a7f2" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="2" data-solution="The y-coordinate represents the number of minutes that Armando swims." data-solution-options="[&quot;The x-coordinate represents the number of minutes that Armando swims.&quot;, &quot;The y-coordinate represents the number of minutes that Armando swims.&quot;, &quot;The solution represents a workout which allows Armando to burn at least 500 calories.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>12. Which of the following is true about the solution you found in the previous question?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The problem states that y represents the number of minutes Armando swims.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.12.2 and 2.12.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
